   1:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c **** /**
   2:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****   ******************************************************************************
   3:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****   * @file    stm32f4xx_dac.c
   4:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****   * @author  MCD Application Team
   5:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****   * @version V1.8.0
   6:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****   * @date    04-November-2016
   7:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****    * @brief   This file provides firmware functions to manage the following 
   8:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****   *          functionalities of the Digital-to-Analog Converter (DAC) peripheral: 
   9:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****   *           + DAC channels configuration: trigger, output buffer, data format
  10:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****   *           + DMA management      
  11:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****   *           + Interrupts and flags management
  12:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****   *
  13:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****  @verbatim      
  14:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****  ===============================================================================
  15:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****                       ##### DAC Peripheral features #####
  16:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****  ===============================================================================
  17:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****     [..]        
  18:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****       *** DAC Channels ***
  19:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****       ====================  
  20:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****     [..]  
  21:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****     The device integrates two 12-bit Digital Analog Converters that can 
  22:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****     be used independently or simultaneously (dual mode):
  23:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****       (#) DAC channel1 with DAC_OUT1 (PA4) as output
  24:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****       (#) DAC channel2 with DAC_OUT2 (PA5) as output
  25:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****   
  26:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****       *** DAC Triggers ***
  27:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****       ====================
  28:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****     [..]
  29:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****     Digital to Analog conversion can be non-triggered using DAC_Trigger_None
  30:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****     and DAC_OUT1/DAC_OUT2 is available once writing to DHRx register 
ARM GAS  /tmp/ccfksLCM.s 			page 2


  31:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****     using DAC_SetChannel1Data() / DAC_SetChannel2Data() functions.
  32:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****     [..] 
  33:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****     Digital to Analog conversion can be triggered by:
  34:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****       (#) External event: EXTI Line 9 (any GPIOx_Pin9) using DAC_Trigger_Ext_IT9.
  35:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****           The used pin (GPIOx_Pin9) must be configured in input mode.
  36:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****   
  37:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****       (#) Timers TRGO: TIM2, TIM4, TIM5, TIM6, TIM7 and TIM8 
  38:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****           (DAC_Trigger_T2_TRGO, DAC_Trigger_T4_TRGO...)
  39:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****           The timer TRGO event should be selected using TIM_SelectOutputTrigger()
  40:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****   
  41:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****       (#) Software using DAC_Trigger_Software
  42:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****   
  43:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****       *** DAC Buffer mode feature ***
  44:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****       =============================== 
  45:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****       [..] 
  46:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****       Each DAC channel integrates an output buffer that can be used to 
  47:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****       reduce the output impedance, and to drive external loads directly
  48:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****       without having to add an external operational amplifier.
  49:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****       To enable, the output buffer use  
  50:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****       DAC_InitStructure.DAC_OutputBuffer = DAC_OutputBuffer_Enable;
  51:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****       [..]           
  52:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****       (@) Refer to the device datasheet for more details about output 
  53:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****           impedance value with and without output buffer.
  54:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****             
  55:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****        *** DAC wave generation feature ***
  56:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****        =================================== 
  57:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****        [..]     
  58:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****        Both DAC channels can be used to generate
  59:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****          (#) Noise wave using DAC_WaveGeneration_Noise
  60:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****          (#) Triangle wave using DAC_WaveGeneration_Triangle
  61:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****           
  62:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****           -@-  Wave generation can be disabled using DAC_WaveGeneration_None
  63:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****   
  64:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****        *** DAC data format ***
  65:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****        =======================
  66:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****        [..]   
  67:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****        The DAC data format can be:
  68:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****          (#) 8-bit right alignment using DAC_Align_8b_R
  69:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****          (#) 12-bit left alignment using DAC_Align_12b_L
  70:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****          (#) 12-bit right alignment using DAC_Align_12b_R
  71:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****   
  72:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****        *** DAC data value to voltage correspondence ***  
  73:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****        ================================================ 
  74:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****        [..] 
  75:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****        The analog output voltage on each DAC channel pin is determined
  76:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****        by the following equation: 
  77:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****        DAC_OUTx = VREF+ * DOR / 4095
  78:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****        with  DOR is the Data Output Register
  79:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****           VEF+ is the input voltage reference (refer to the device datasheet)
  80:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****         e.g. To set DAC_OUT1 to 0.7V, use
  81:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****           DAC_SetChannel1Data(DAC_Align_12b_R, 868);
  82:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****           Assuming that VREF+ = 3.3V, DAC_OUT1 = (3.3 * 868) / 4095 = 0.7V
  83:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****   
  84:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****        *** DMA requests  ***
  85:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****        =====================
  86:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****        [..]    
  87:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****        A DMA1 request can be generated when an external trigger (but not
ARM GAS  /tmp/ccfksLCM.s 			page 3


  88:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****        a software trigger) occurs if DMA1 requests are enabled using
  89:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****        DAC_DMACmd()
  90:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****        [..]
  91:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****        DMA1 requests are mapped as following:
  92:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****          (#) DAC channel1 : mapped on DMA1 Stream5 channel7 which must be 
  93:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****              already configured
  94:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****          (#) DAC channel2 : mapped on DMA1 Stream6 channel7 which must be 
  95:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****              already configured
  96:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****   
  97:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****       
  98:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****                       ##### How to use this driver #####
  99:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****  ===============================================================================
 100:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****     [..]          
 101:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****       (+) DAC APB clock must be enabled to get write access to DAC
 102:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****           registers using
 103:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****           RCC_APB1PeriphClockCmd(RCC_APB1Periph_DAC, ENABLE)
 104:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****       (+) Configure DAC_OUTx (DAC_OUT1: PA4, DAC_OUT2: PA5) in analog mode.
 105:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****       (+) Configure the DAC channel using DAC_Init() function
 106:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****       (+) Enable the DAC channel using DAC_Cmd() function
 107:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****    
 108:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****  @endverbatim    
 109:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_dac.c ****   ******************************************************************************
